# Part III — Consolidation: significance run in reverse (the legibility side)

*Designed with Rohan 2026-07-17. Parts I–II GENERATE meaning — they add derivations and, in the corpus loop,
promote rules: **σ-accumulation**. Part III is the same invariant run backwards — given the accumulated
structure, PRUNE it to raise the signal-to-noise of what remains, so meaning becomes more **legible**. This is
not a second problem; it is the other side of the one problem. Two of its theorems are already machine-checked
(inherited from the Specification-Complexity paper and transported); the thermodynamic version is CONJECTURE,
marked as such.*

17. Safe forgetting = σ-preserving reduction

The engine accumulates drift as it reads: reflexive parse junk (`woman —anger→ woman`), ungrounded generic
subjects, terminal dead-ends, and — across the corpus loop — over-general or oscillating induced rules (§16.6).
§§1–16 weigh, rank, and promote; none of them FORGET. The question Part III answers is when forgetting is SAFE —
when a piece of accumulated structure can be dropped with a *proof* that no meaning was lost.

The Specification-Complexity paper supplies the answer, and it is not a metaphor. σ is invariant under any
transformation that preserves the mutation structure (**representation independence**, SC Thm 2.3,
machine-checked): the whole space of structures with the same kill-profile is one you may move within freely, so
reducing to the *simplest member* of that space loses nothing. And a constraint is REDUNDANT iff it contributes
zero information gain — it distinguishes no alternative the rest already distinguish (**redundancy
characterization**, SC Thm 3.11, machine-checked). Transport the nouns exactly as SSL does (program → a text's
meaning; mutant → a candidate reading; killing test → the derivation that fixes a reading): **a spine edit is
SAFE to forget iff it preserves the significance-weighted closure** — iff re-deriving after the prune leaves the
σ_sem-witness (the high-κ, spine-clean survivors) unchanged. What banks zero significance-weighted coverage is,
by Thm 3.11 transported, exactly what can be forgotten *with proof*.

This is not a new capability — it is one the substrate already performs on CODE. Detective's `decompose --apply`
throws away a tangled implementation and keeps whatever preserves the mutant-kill witness, applying the refactor
only when the preservation is PROVEN behaviour-identical. Consolidation is that same operator run OFFLINE over
accumulated MEANING, and its parts already exist: `retraction.recompute_retraction` is the precise
derivation-DAG undo (one prune, exact re-derivation); the significance layer (`κ` / `chain_significance` /
`_spine_noise`) is the invariant; §14 admissibility is the well-definedness guard on what may be touched. §6's
finding that the S/N resolution is SPINE-INHERENT — structural, not corpus statistics — is what makes this
legible-by-construction: one may PROVABLY forget what the spine floor already marks as noise, because it banks no
significance-weighted coverage.

17.1 Wake and sleep are the two directions of the σ-dynamics

SC §3 is the FORWARD trajectory: greedy accumulation of constraints, with the bulk→tail phase transition
(statistical → exact learning, SC Thm 3.4). Read in reverse, it is the shape of consolidation:

- **Waking** (active reading) is the forward greedy trajectory — add derivations, accumulate the BULK:
  correlated, redundant, drift-laden coverage.
- **Sleep** is redundancy-elimination back to the σ-minimal witness — strip the bulk that Thm 3.11 certifies as
  zero-information, keep the independent TAIL, where the meaning-bearing degrees of freedom live.

The neuroscience prior this makes rigorous is Crick & Mitchison's **reverse-learning** theory of dreams (1983):
dreams prune spurious/parasitic attractors. The transported theorems turn their conjecture into a definition — a
spurious memory *is* a zero-κ derivation, and reverse-learning *is* greedy σ-reduction under a preserved witness.
It is also the cleanest bridge to the György et al. (2025) thesis Part I invokes: forgetting the statistical bulk
to keep the exact tail is precisely the statistical→exact transition (SC Thm 3.4) enacted offline — consolidation
is where an approximate, drift-heavy read is compressed to its exactly-identifying core.

17.2 Status: proved / transported / conjectured, and the Lean targets

- **PROVED (inherited, machine-checked — cite, do not re-derive):** representation independence (SC Thm 2.3);
  redundancy = zero information gain (SC Thm 3.11); greedy redundancy ratio zero.
- **ASSERTED (this part's transport — the Lean targets, provable on the Wayfinder/Aristotle pipeline):**
  1. `safe_forget_preserves_sigma_sem` — a spine edit that changes no significance-weighted survivor preserves
     the read's σ_sem-witness (the transport of 2.3/3.11 to the meaning closure; the honest core of Part III).
  2. `consolidation_terminates` — repeated safe-forgetting descends a finite, monotone structure (the closure
     only shrinks, only zero-κ elements are removed), so it reaches a fixpoint: the σ-minimal legible read.
- **CONJECTURE (needs the SSL H-series wired here — the same gap as §16.5's `L_ind`):** that consolidation
  MINIMIZES a specification FREE ENERGY (SC Thm 3.10 — greedy specification is variational inference), i.e.
  "sleep as inference." Promising, at the tier of §11–§13, not built.

**In one line.** Parts I–II make meaning; Part III makes it LEGIBLE — the same σ, run in reverse, forgetting
exactly what a machine-checked theorem certifies carries none.

