The resumed BODY worklist first checked the sixteen original questions against the joint candidate. Twelve already had supported zeros. The four still open belonged to the ten reviewed anatomical-standard exceptions. A bounded, Zipf-ordered typed probe obtained ten positive BODY answers. Each answer was checked against the exact exception source before the completion writer regenerated its request and consumed the saved answer. This separates a disputed model ruling from the independently reviewed definition that warrants a replacement. [Resumption plan](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-11-lexicon-learning-loop/unit-banks-probe-plan.json), [exception reviews](../../../../gse/docs/readings/2026-11-11-lexicon-learning-loop/body-exception-model-review.json)

